      "id": "ukrq667",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Foundation of the Delhi Sultanate"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Delhi Sultanate comprised five major dynasties: Slave (Mamluk), Khilji, Tughlaq, Sayyid, and Lodi.",
        "Extensive administrative and revenue systems were established to govern vast territories across Northern India.",
        "Indo-Islamic architectural traditions evolved significantly across different dynastic phases.",
        "Sultanate governance brought prominent shifts in trade, agrarian economy, and urban society."
      ],
      "id": "vqkyqjr"
    },
